{"title":"Subjectwise Test-10 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 EE Digital Electronics","fileName":"029_Subjectwise Test-10 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 EE Digital Electronics.html","branch":"ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2026 + GATE 2025 Online Test Series Electrical Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":5400,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,D","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the circuit shown in the figure,</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/99585c598086e7ad92eca5077716746e972e1c51.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n Which of the following statement is correct about the circuit?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n Output <em>Y</em> = 0, when <em>A</em> = 0 and <em>B</em> = 0</p>\n</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n Output <em>Y</em> = 1, when <em>A</em> = 1 and <em>B</em> = 0</p>\n</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n Output <em>Y</em> = 1, for all this inputs</p>\n</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n Output <em>Y</em> = 0, for <em>A</em> = 1 and <em>B</em> = 0</p>\n</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a, d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/34e06aa5e4d6cc5d92fe0ff274838df2ef547d84.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n The digital circuit shown in figure has two 3-bit inputs <em>A</em><sub>2</sub> <em>A</em><sub>1</sub> <em>A</em><sub>0</sub> and <em>B</em><sub>2</sub> <em>B</em><sub>1</sub> <em>B</em><sub>0</sub> .</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/87a1e674843dc987c8494a02eceb05ed772eb303.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n To obtain output <em>Y</em> = 1, the number of possible cases is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 16</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 32</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 48</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 64</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/7eb78a8a97df2d1af59682ad05b7edf1962a280f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/5e50504cfd9cd023fa3fcec3c1bcd79e09a56f4b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n </p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the following circuit:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/f28df6e78bc344b2b2e35d48d08b793b6a3a6fce.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n Which one of the following gives the function implemented by the MUX-based digital circuit?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/96d90cdbea1bf299585bb02260e7ffa1f1b15224.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/ce66bd123773133ca9a52c6c5f347efa15b1e00b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/c25fb8d28c62e18443cf92d34832470810371034.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/3a8e64b875055f049533681ad161bac64b9bf2a8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/d2fd1d294492d4f9b80ec6a61d0823006e60fbd0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":4,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n The boolean expression for the logic diagram shown in figure is</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/c413868269738f392043140261af2616751e8d08.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>AC</em></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>AB</em></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>ABC</em></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>BC</em></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/8feae