"D","text":"<div> 6.25 V</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/854bdfd7516dd45506a687a9efa752e097b9dd88.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":8,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n If <img src=\"/media/63508218fef40fe47c6a74ee57e17ce6912a8b34.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>Y</em></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 0</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 1</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/c259700dd17cba1d3e68d837610a772140fab31b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/0334610793c4a3c9786026f3931c6d09f731bd59.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":9,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n The following truth table has to be realized with the circuit shown in figure,</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/5c8277df0a150c55021017e13778036d9f509266.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/32b7932398fc0bbea40a5ae882f0989aacdadc12.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n What is the output of the combinational logic circuit to the J-input ?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/9ec11a7085fbac4b88bf8d6521b4c921a6116575.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>AB</em></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/c84cfceb05d6888d8bb44b607ffca238ee5b280c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/4c962b3744b3ff7c73775a0e30655e32986090fc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/d35ed9614826a110ae5b42dc3c6b80f1b4db5ced.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":10,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n The Boolean function <em>f</em>(<em>A</em>, <em>B</em>, <em>C</em>) = <img src=\"/media/167f0273c27fa92691a1907786b5dd06696de74c.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is to be implemented by using 4 : 1 MUX having select lines <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> = <em>B</em> and <em>S</em><sub>0</sub> = <em>C</em>.</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/b57b2770ed3b68d67dbb2659f5f3cb5c79312510.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The required inputs <img src=\"/media/8743d45321254c058aa1af3a7de9e2b5ebb3f73f.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> respectively are</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/92e14f6d6e790c260f896f9be33f710a60c8e873.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/6f4e22be7826ab0f5796cf9e4ff8a39315b85170.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/2895d4c6abaf15339f836102e672c579501f97e2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/28ecd8f94f90fc47875f6e70b6b0e2e0c9411e07.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/beda99bb418c97964db9a216cbf44d239aa7a43b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":11,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n A two input gate having inputs ‘<em>A</em>’ and ‘<em>B</em>’ is implemented using 4 : 1 MUX as shown in the figure below.</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/988cde0fa55bf47fa4ee7e58bcb9396497e15452.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n Then the minimum number of two input NAND gates required to implement the same expression as output (Y) of MUX is equal to ______.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"3","high":"3"},"solution":"<p>\n 3</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/5102fa5510efedaf2ee18cf1101a55c20f907766.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":12,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the combinational circuit shown below:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/992060aa6b80200ccd25ec04dca7fc19b370b549.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The minimum number of 2 input NAND gates required to implement the above set of equations for <em>A</em> and <em>B</em> is _______ .</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"5","high":"5"},"solution":"<p>\n 5</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/7c8867bc00b03c1aa26042079da11c74936dc4be.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/1e6df713ec860d291b2537d6f8e1ad08b7f82e53.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":13,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n A 10 bit A/D converter is used to digitalize an analog signal in the 0 to 5 V range. The maximum peak to peak ripple voltage that can be allowed in the D.C. supply voltage is equal to ________ mV.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"4.75","high":"5"},"solution":"<p>\n 4.88 (4.75 - 5.00)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/09bab44870a06633c8794ae1a98fd0db2f38d9fb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":14,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the state diagram shown below.</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/0210aca88fba8071852db2f75e648063a52ccaba.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n Then which of the following statements is incorrect?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> The machine produces an output 1 when exactly two 0’s are followed by 1.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> The machine produces an output 1 when exactly two 1’s are followed by 0.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> The reduced state table will contain only five states.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> The minimum number of flip-flop required to implement this machine is equal to four.</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/8aee5bd42f1cad30f0aa52840b05d3fffbb70ab8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n </p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":15,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the logic circuit shown in figure:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/133a6a45fbf4e2bd5395c7cd6f2b52ad29d151fc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The number of NAND gates required to implement the output function Y is equal to ________ .</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0","high":"0"},"solution":"<p>\n 0</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/1a687c74f7925b55bf7f348a78ed86f829998007.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":16,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the following circuit</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/65ebf3dad5bdd1ec38e35d62bcbde8f1d57e4863.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n Initially the counter is at “000”. After 9 clock pulses, the state of LEDs is<br />\n (assume +<em>V<sub>CC</sub></em> and 0 are used to represent logic-1 and logic-0 respectively)</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> only LED1 and LED 2 are ON</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> only LED 2 and LED 3 are ON</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> only LED 1 and LED 3 are ON</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> All LED’s are ON</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (c)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/e4c85921c5c5f16047fa94356a7f0fbb417aa522.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":17,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider a sequential circuit using three J-K flip-flops and one AND gate as shown in figure.<br />\n Output (z) of the circuit becomes ‘1’ after every <em>N</em>-clock cycles. The value of <em>N</em> is _________ .</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/58d9eeceb9fbf7b42b7a4873b82f501720e0cba3.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"6","high":"6"},"solution":"<p>\n 6</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/698ec80eac8ea59f995e586a93982af1134bbfb4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":18,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n If the input of a DAC is changed from 0111110100 to 0111111001 then output voltage change is 25 mV. Then the full scale reading of DAC is ________ V.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"5.1","high":"5.13"},"solution":"<p>\n 5.12 (5.10 - 5.13)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/9ac1345f4e13b76a8a7b86a7dfd5bb7bbf56ed79.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":19,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the following circuit involving a positive edge triggered <em>D</em> Flip-flop.</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/58d305961e355d7fe0040cfe1c09b3704cc799ad.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n Consider the following timing diagram. Let <img src=\"/media/958413ac7a340cbf194b0e05d70bf968263384b7.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> represent the logic level on the line A in the <img src=\"/media/8f572f7970901cb2d1e48956f86e7e257671ca55.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> clock period.</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/4be1cfdbbda95c926dcaf1914a75960d9acf5d31.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n Let A′ represent the complement of A. The correct output sequence on Y over the clock periods 1 through 5 is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n A<sub>0</sub> A<sub>1</sub> A<sub>1</sub>′ A<sub>3</sub> A<sub>4</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n A<sub>0</sub> A<sub>1</sub> A<sub>2</sub>′ A<sub>3</sub> A<sub>4</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n A<sub>1</sub> A<sub>2</sub> A<sub>2</sub> ′ A<sub>3</sub> A<sub>4</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n A<sub>1</sub> A<sub>2</sub> ′ A<sub>3</sub> A<sub>4</sub> A<sub>5</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (a)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/ad532186cd011e7acacc4f9d509b9660001cb5fa.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/41c2aad01af2197c27bbc683abd7903542bf71a2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":20,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the circuit shown in the figure:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/681e929c08e2d7a524c7e8570ffc3c1767ae3fb8.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n If the input clock frequency is equal to 6 MHz, then the output signal frequency is equal to ________ kHz.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"2000","high":"2000"},"solution":"<p>\n 2000</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/1b1885c3932d83d8efaadf53129a78b9508fd837.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":21,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n If a 32 kHz clock is to be converted into 100 Hz clock signal using a ripple counter followed by a Johnson counter both using same number of flip flops, then the total number of flip-flops used in the circuit will be _________.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"10","high":"10"},"solution":"<p>\n 10 (10 - 10)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/2746523eabf8c04933ecbf3b04e85bc0c109ae73.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":22,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the circuit shown in figure:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/a8ba053792cacedf751aef095fb28bf0608f6056.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The minimized expression for <em>F</em>(<em>X</em>, <em>Y</em>, <em>Z</em>) is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/8c381ae0268938577b404415407c4d48a9f19d46.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/a227e27911d2e3cf9980c48aadb43db66316c270.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/91e5b7e98a4ef75956cc198a7474e69575ff839c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/4d0e3931cad454f571ae4e138d340822eb84b2f9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (d)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/6a58126d819aef3145f890ae37e6d3346badde70.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":23,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n The following circuit has two flip-flops and two blocks of combinational logic with the indicated timing specifications:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/31e8372682d9854ca8f4e7db3b69a0fe9c2191d2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n Assume that the clock period is 25 ns, then the maximum setup time for the flip-flops for which this circuit will operate correctly will be ________ ns.</p>\n<p>\n (Answer upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"7.95","high":"8.05"},"solution":"<p>\n 8.00 (7.95 - 8.05)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/ea29023b46682d633e34e85c67d4185e0028abeb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":24,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the 4 : 1 MUX based circuit as shown in the figure. <em>A</em> and <em>B</em> are two periodic signals with duty cycles 25% and 50% respectively as given in the figure. If +5 V and 0 V are used to represent logic-1 and logic-0 respectively, then the average power dissipated by the resistor <em>R<sub>L </sub></em>will be _________ mW.</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/f2fe3c3b5177877b253e17ccb8c51664efe39cfc.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"6.2","high":"6.3"},"solution":"<p>\n 6.25 (6.20 - 6.3