"Technical"},{"qnum":27,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n The number of clock pulses needed to change the contents of an 8-bit up-counter from (10111001)<sub>2 </sub>to (01001110)<sub>2</sub> is ________.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"149","high":"149"},"solution":"<p>\n 149</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/a8c7ff9d1e66888634065c85e5a5a27e457effd5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":28,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>\n Consider the state diagram shown in the figure:</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/cdc6b7ddb6ca71300d145da589123018108f5b08.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>\n The 4-bit sequence circuit is used to detect (_____)<sub>2</sub>.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"1111","high":"1111"},"solution":"<p>\n 1111</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/4df27fb42ae411130d591e4f8733e650c837304a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":29,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>\n The logic expression <img src=\"/media/8813379655c0c0d2bec5b2269dc5338795792d19.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> is equal to</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/eb3de0ccbc933f6e6491d28f81acdf40655bab78.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/ca589630c3353a0c1ef1881b94040bf679f30bc2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/e83b943068ad7ab8a803bf96bb2a5c20950352ac.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/d1b1952579db4d3f081ca77071bf441194e364c6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>\n (b)</p>\n<p>\n <img src=\"/media/aa760558714520dc3ec23ef3c5c32c9ec8d32c2a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":30,"type":"MC